      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "EEG is the result of brain activity aimed at processing the external and internal information. Intraoperative pain (as a specific type of information) developing because of inadequate anesthesia increases the total amount of information on the EEG. A new original method is proposed for assessing the efficacy of analgesia, based on computer monitoring of information saturation of EEG in the on-line regimen during an operative intervention under combined total anesthesia. Physiological and clinical significance of the detected phenomena is discussed."},
